.TH "SERVICEWORKERGLOBALSCOPE.COOKIECHANGE_EVENT" "3JS" "October 27, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
ServiceWorkerGlobalScope.cookiechange_event \- ServiceWorkerGlobalScope:
cookiechange event
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]Secure context:\f[R] This feature is available only in secure
contexts (HTTPS).
.PP
\f[B]Note:\f[R] This feature is only available in Service Workers.
.PP
The \f[B]\f[CB]cookiechange\f[B]\f[R] event of the
\f[CR]ServiceWorkerGlobalScope\f[R] interface is fired when a cookie
change occurs that matches the service worker\(cqs cookie change
subscription list.
.PP
This event is not cancelable and does not bubble.
.SH SYNTAX
Use the event name in \f[CR]addEventListener()\f[R]:
.IP
.EX
addEventListener(\(dqcookiechange\(dq, (event) => { })
.EE
.PP
Alternatively, assign to the event handler property of the interface:
.IP
.EX
oncookiechange = (event) => { }
.EE
.SH EVENT TYPE
An \f[CR]ExtendableCookieChangeEvent\f[R].
Inherits from \f[CR]ExtendableEvent\f[R].
